Additional attribution (Y11S3 support)

Format knowledge and table data for Y11S3 replays were taken from MIT-licensed forks of
r6-dissect. Their LICENSE files are the unmodified MIT text above ("Copyright (c) 2022
Benjamin Ryan", no further copyright notices); the logic below was re-implemented in
JavaScript and verified against real Y11S3 replays:

- Animuxs/r6-stats-app (MIT), dissect/scoreboard.go, header.go, operator_roles.go, map_string.go:
  scoreboard entity layout (entity id + round-start snapshot, field order), walk-back
  snapshot detection, Solid Snake / Noor operator ids and roles, Fortress/Coastline/Villa/Tower Y10 map ids
  (see scoreboard.js, tables.js).
- prestonwillis10/r6-dissect (MIT), dissect/player.go, header.go: operator swap record layout
  (23 <player object> F93911F2 08 <u64> 22 A9260BE4 08 <operator>) and operator ids
  (see player.js, tables.js).
- prestonwillis10/r6-dissect (MIT), dissect/defuse.go: Y10S4+ defuser packet layout (the timer is a property of the
  acting player's pawn: 23 <pawn> 00000000 E58C06E9 / E9A37FEB, pawn -> slot link 1B <slot> 00000000 27C08DCA <pawn>,
  run/state handling, 0.00 completion, sole-living-player fallback). Re-verified on Y11S3 replays (see defuse.js).
